coi rodo

After a half a year of offline vegetation, I am back to the Net. I
have resubscribed to the list from a new address (in fact it is a very
old address - maybe someone remember me writing from it back in
nineties). But I was not just idle while being offline - I have my
Lojban mode for Vim totally rewritten. Now it does a real job of word
analysis, not just a rough approximation like earlier versions (by the
way, sometimes it doesn't agree with vlatai - it is an open question
which is right). New features of Vim 7.0 are appreciated (and probably
required - I have not tested it against Vim 6.x). Download it from:

    http://45.free.net/~slobin/vim/lojban.zip

There is no separate documentation, but at the top of each file in the
archive there is an exhaustive comment. I believe that if you are
using Vim, you should be smart enough to install this suite! ;-)

